1
00:00:02,903 --> 00:00:04,603
(Bernadette:)I like your suit.

2
00:00:04,605 --> 00:00:07,135
(Penny:)Oh, thanks. Got a couple
new outfits for work.

3
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:09,110
(Howard:)How does it feel knowing
your fiancée's job

4
00:00:09,109 --> 00:00:11,239
(Howard:)is to go out
and flirt with doctors,

5
00:00:11,245 --> 00:00:13,915
(Howard:)looking like that,
while you sit here, you know...

6
00:00:13,914 --> 00:00:15,944
(Howard:)looking like this?

7
00:00:15,949 --> 00:00:18,649
(Leonard:)She doesn't flirt
with doctors.

8
00:00:18,652 --> 00:00:20,782
(Penny:)Yeah. It's all
very professional.

9
00:00:20,787 --> 00:00:22,817
(Amy:)You know when you bend over,
I can see down your shirt?

10
00:00:22,823 --> 00:00:24,623
(Penny:)Okay, good.

11
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:27,225
(Bernadette:)Speaking of new careers,
how are things going

12
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:29,257
(Bernadette:)with dark matter,
Sheldon?

13
00:00:29,263 --> 00:00:31,893
(Sheldon:)Oh, yeah, I'd have to say
it's the most exiting time

14
00:00:31,899 --> 00:00:33,629
(Sheldon:)in the history of the field.
Oh.

15
00:00:33,634 --> 00:00:34,664
(Bernadette:)What's going on?

16
00:00:34,668 --> 00:00:37,268
(Sheldon:)I started doing it.

17
00:00:37,271 --> 00:00:38,471
KOOTHRAPPALI:
You know, the government funded

18
00:00:38,472 --> 00:00:41,172
(Raj:)the biggest experiment yet
to detect dark matter.

19
00:00:41,174 --> 00:00:42,644
(Sheldon:)Oh, yeah,

20
00:00:42,643 --> 00:00:44,873
(Leonard:)I've read about that--
they're sending research teams

21
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:47,348
(Leonard:)down into abandoned salt mines.
You know, Sheldon,

22
00:00:47,347 --> 00:00:49,517
(Raj:)if we apply to be
one of those teams,

23
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,986
(Raj:)we could be
on the ground floor
of something big--

24
00:00:51,985 --> 00:00:54,655
(Raj:)not just for theoretical physics
but for astrophysics as well.

25
00:00:54,655 --> 00:00:57,685
(Penny:)Wait, hang on-- you guys
are gonna work in a mine?

26
00:00:57,691 --> 00:00:58,861
(Sheldon:)Why not?
You had

27
00:00:58,859 --> 00:01:01,829
(Penny:)a panic attack when
we went through the car wash.

28
00:01:01,828 --> 00:01:04,768
(Sheldon:)Perhaps the emotion
you're referring to was shock

29
00:01:04,765 --> 00:01:07,235
(Sheldon:)at you having something cleaned.

30
00:01:08,435 --> 00:01:10,665
(Leonard:)I think what Penny meant is,
the thought of you two

31
00:01:10,671 --> 00:01:14,371
(Leonard:)in a mine is kind of funny--
it's like a cat riding a Roomba.

32
00:01:14,374 --> 00:01:15,444
(laughs)

33
00:01:15,442 --> 00:01:17,012
(Howard:)If they get scared,
they'll have those hats

34
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:18,640
(Howard:)with the lights on them,
'cause down there

35
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:21,415
it's night-night all the time!

36
00:01:21,415 --> 00:01:22,445
(Bernadette:)Maybe they could

37
00:01:22,449 --> 00:01:24,579
(Bernadette:)ride around in one of
those mine carts that go,

38
00:01:24,585 --> 00:01:27,215
(squeakily):
ee-oo-ee-oo-ee-oo.

39
00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:31,190
(Leonard:)Yeah, it'll help them get away
when they see a gh-gh-ghost...!

40
00:01:32,092 --> 00:01:34,792
(Sheldon:)Are they making
fun of us?
Yup.

41
00:01:34,795 --> 00:01:38,025
(Sheldon:)I miss the old days
when I couldn't tell.

